#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently asked Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1152
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I add my own custom service menus to &dolphin;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Dolphin can use the majority of service menus created for Konqueror, however "
"&dolphin; does impose one limitation on the service menus: Service menu "
"entries that add them selves to the top level of the context menu will "
"automatically be placed below the Actions sub-menu. This prevents that the "
"context menu will get crowded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a custom service menu to &dolphin; save the service menu to the "
"&dolphin; service menu directory, this can be found in /home/house/.kde/"
"share/apps/dolphin/servicemenus/. If the servicemenus sub-directory does not "
"exist in the &dolphin; directory, then create the sub-directory and save the "
"service menu to that directory. The next time the user launch &dolphin; the "
"service menu will be available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1167
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I make Dolphin my default file manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To make &dolphin; the default file manager for &kde; from the &kde; control "
"centre open the File Associations section via; KDE Components>File "
"Associations. If the user adds &dolphin; to the list of applications for the "
"directory mime type and make it the first choice, then &dolphin; will become "
"the default application to open any directory with. The directory mime type "
"can be found by expanding the inode section of Known Types."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To make &dolphin; the default file manager for the virtual directories &kde; "
"creates e.g. system:/ then again in the File Associations section of the "
"control centre expand the inode section of Known Types. Under the "
"system_directory mime type, add &dolphin; to the list of applications, "
"however instead of choosing &dolphin; from the kmenu, type the following in "
"to the text box at the top; dolphin %u The virtual directories created by "
"&kde; will then be opened by &dolphin; as default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Miscellaneous Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Does Dolphin intended to replace Konqueror?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is not intended to be a competitor to Konqueror: Konqueror acts as "
"universal viewer being able to show HTML pages, text documents, directories "
"and a lot more, whereas &dolphin; focuses on being only a file manager. This "
"approach allows to optimize the user interface for the task of file "
"management."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Will Dolphin be ported to Kde4?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Development of &dolphin; for Kde4 is scheduled to begin in December (2006). "
"These are just intial ideas floating around at the moment between the "
"developers. By the time the first alpha release of Kde4 is released, then "
"&dolphin; devlopment should be well underway."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1212
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I get involved with the development of Dolphin?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get involved with &dolphin; is to drop the developers an "
"email. If you email Peter Penz (Lead Developer/Project Leader), what you can "
"do, how much time you can devote etc and he will let you know what you can "
"do in the project. If you wish to contribute the documentation email Michael "
"Austin (Documentation Leader). He can then fill you in on the situation e.g. "
"what needs to be added/finished, the procedure for submitting documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The email addresses of Peter Penz and Michael Austin can be found on the "
"main page of the documentation, or in the Credits section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I submit bug reports to?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Bug reports should only be submitted for release versions of &dolphin;, "
"please do not submit bug reports for the Subversion release of &dolphin; as "
"this is expected to break due to it's constant development."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
